0033: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0034:     """
0035:     Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.
0036: 
0037:     Input structure:
0038:     - Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.
0039:     - Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).
0040: 
0041:     Rule:
0042:     - Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.
0043:     - Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.
0044:     - Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.
0045:     - Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.
0046: 
0047:     Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.
